<title>AUSTRALIA: Trade union warns of widening Email dispute.</title>
<headline>Trade union warns of widening Email dispute.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade unionists have warned that a dispute with manufacturer Email Ltd could escalate across the state of Victoria if it does not take a &quot;realistic&quot; position in wage talks.</p>
<p>Five of Email's plants in Victoria are beset by industrial action after trade unions and management failed to find common ground in negotiations for new site-specific deals on wages.</p>
<p>The Australian Manufacturing Workers Union (AMWU), which wants a 15 percent pay rise over two years for its members at Email sites, said on Monday the company had offered only two to four percent a year.</p>
</text>
